## 🏗️ Invoice Automation — Architecture Plan

### What it does

A **SharePoint file-drop trigger** fires when a new PDF lands in your folder. The flow downloads the file, runs it through the **`InvoiceIXP`** extraction model (already published on your tenant) to pull out invoice number, vendor name, date, total, and line items, then maps those fields into a SAP payload and posts the invoice directly into SAP — fully automated.

### Flow Diagram

```mermaid
graph LR
    fileTrigger(SharePoint File Created)
    getFile[Get File from SharePoint]
    extractInvoice[InvoiceIXP Extract Fields]
    mapFields[Map Fields to SAP Payload]
    postToSap[SAP Post Invoice]
    doneSuccess(Done)
    terminateFatal(Fatal Error)
    fileTrigger -->|output| getFile
    getFile -->|output| extractInvoice
    getFile -->|error| terminateFatal
    extractInvoice -->|success| mapFields
    extractInvoice -->|error| terminateFatal
    mapFields -->|success| postToSap
    mapFields -->|error| terminateFatal
    postToSap -->|output| doneSuccess
    postToSap -->|error| terminateFatal
```

### Node Summary

| # | Node | What it does |
|---|------|-------------|
| 1 | **SharePoint File Created** | Connector trigger — polls OneDrive/SharePoint for new PDFs in your folder |
| 2 | **Get File from SharePoint** | Downloads the PDF content to feed into extraction |
| 3 | **InvoiceIXP Extract Fields** | IxP extraction model — pulls invoice number, vendor, date, total, line items |
| 4 | **Map Fields to SAP Payload** | Script node — reshapes extracted fields into the SAP BAPI input format |
| 5 | **Post Invoice to SAP** | SAP BAPI connector — executes `BAPI_INCOMINGINVOICE_CREATE` (or equivalent) |
| 6 | **Done** | Happy-path end |
| 7 | **Fatal Error (Terminate)** | Catches any failure from any step — ensures nothing silently passes |

---

